<Callout title="Guide scope: job change to level 130" tone="warning">
  <p><strong>This guide follows your progression from the Revenant job change all the way to Base Level 130.</strong> Beyond level 130, most locations require specific equipment and setups. Use this foundation to explore, adapt your build, and choose your own route.</p>
</Callout>

<h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
<p>Revenant is Trickster's final evolution, continuing its STR/LUK scythe build with area attacks, life leech, and a barrier generated by overhealing. Sustained attacks keep both damage and recovery flowing. Crowd control, ranged attacks, and lingering ground damage are its main weaknesses.</p>
<Callout title="Refuge Changes">
  <ul><li>Ominous Presence converts excess scythe leech into a shield at 3% per skill level.</li><li>Flaming Wave has no cast time and its Burning duration is five times longer.</li><li>Final Orchestra heals 1% of maximum HP per pulse per skill level, damaging and knocking back Undead and Demon enemies for half the healing amount.</li></ul>
</Callout>
<h2 id="job-change">Job Change Quest</h2>
<Callout title="Requirement: Trickster Job Level 70">
  <ol>
    <li>Speak to the <strong>Recluse Trickster</strong> in Niflheim at <strong>niflheim 93, 227</strong>. Ask for an audience with Lady Hel.</li>
    <li>Follow Serin through the Long Night and defeat the corrupted Reapers at <strong>que_sign01 49, 27</strong>.</li>
    <li>Defeat <strong>Revenant Ebel</strong> at <strong>que_sign01 55, 217</strong>.</li>
    <li>Survive Lady Hel's ritual at <strong>que_sign01 45, 227</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p><strong>Rewards:</strong> the Revenant job, a Reaper egg, and a reforged scythe. Hatch the egg for a combat pet that grants leech and inflicts Burning, or exchange it for a Revenant Ebel Card for Critical Rate and Critical Damage.</p>
</Callout>
<h2 id="core-gameplay">Core Gameplay &amp; Skills</h2>
<ul>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="LG_MOONSLASHER" /><strong>Reaping Slash:</strong> your new combo filler and Overslash stack builder. Hits a 5 × 5 area; building past one stack requires <strong>Combo Ready</strong>. With at least one stack and <strong>Combo Ready</strong> active, <strong>Finisher Ready</strong> lets it maximize stacks immediately.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="LG_OVERBRAND" /><strong>Roaring Overslash:</strong> your main damage nuke. Hits a 7 × 7 area, with an extra hit per Overslash stack. Keep <strong>Combo Ready</strong> active to avoid reduced damage. Both slash skills can critically hit.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="WM_SEVERE_RAINSTORM" /><strong>Underworld Rainstorm:</strong> spends a Shadow Orb on sustained area damage. It never misses and its cast cannot be interrupted, but your defenses are halved while casting.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="KN_SPEARMASTERY" /><strong>Advanced Scythe Mastery:</strong> improves scythe damage and lets <SkillIcon icon="KN_PIERCE" />Sweeping Slash grant <strong>Combo Ready</strong> for three seconds.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="GS_SINGLEACTION" /><strong>Ominous Presence:</strong> improves scythe leech and converts excess healing at full HP into a shield. New overhealing refreshes its 30-second duration.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="KG_KAGEMUSYA" /><strong>Darkside Shadow:</strong> summons a shadow that repeats normal attacks, enabling Double Attack with a scythe. It also improves physical skill damage through DEX scaling; Underworld Rainstorm receives half the bonus.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="GN_BLOOD_SUCKER" /><strong>Vampire Mark:</strong> grants physical-damage leech to yourself or an ally. It stacks with equipment leech and works with Ominous Presence's overheal shield. It does not apply to magic damage.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Utility skills</h3>
<ul>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="TK_HIGHJUMP" /><strong>High Jump:</strong> leap forward over walls and obstacles when the destination cell is accessible. Higher levels increase range and shorten the cast. Requires Darkside Shadow level 1.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="GC_DARKILLUSION" /><strong>Haunting Slice:</strong> closes the gap and attacks a target. Unlock it after Roaring Overslash level 1.</li>
  <li><SkillIcon icon="RK_PHANTOMTHRUST" /><strong>Phantom Slice:</strong> pulls a distant enemy toward you; it can also pull a party member without damaging them.</li>
</ul>
<h3>Stat allocation</h3>
<Callout title="Adjust stats to your build">
  <p>The allocation below is an example, not a requirement. Adjust your stats to suit your skills, equipment, and survivability needs.</p>
</Callout>
<div class="gear-table-wrap"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Stage</th><th>Stats</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td>Before Darkside Shadow</td><td>70 STR, 90 LUK; split points between VIT and INT.</td><td>Continue Trickster's allocation for HP and SP.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>After Darkside Shadow<br />Base Level 130</td><td>99 STR, 90 LUK, 90 DEX, 25 INT.</td><td>Higher Ominous Presence and Darkside Shadow levels allow more reliance on the overheal shield and fewer points in VIT.</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<h3>Skill allocation</h3>
<ol>
  <li>Unlock <SkillIcon icon="LG_OVERBRAND" />Roaring Overslash.</li>
  <li>Max <SkillIcon icon="KN_SPEARMASTERY" />Advanced Scythe Mastery.</li>
  <li>Max <SkillIcon icon="GS_SINGLEACTION" />Ominous Presence.</li>
  <li>Max <SkillIcon icon="KG_KAGEMUSYA" />Darkside Shadow.</li>
  <li>Max <SkillIcon icon="GN_BLOOD_SUCKER" />Vampire Mark.</li>
  <li>Max <SkillIcon icon="LG_OVERBRAND" />Roaring Overslash.</li>
  <li>Spend remaining Job Level skill points on <SkillIcon icon="GC_DARKILLUSION" />Haunting Slice, <SkillIcon icon="TK_HIGHJUMP" />High Jump, or <SkillIcon icon="WM_SEVERE_RAINSTORM" />Underworld Rainstorm, or max <SkillIcon icon="LG_MOONSLASHER" />Reaping Slash.</li>
</ol>
<SourceScreenshot image={{ src: 'images/classes/revenant-owner-skill-tree.png', width: 556, height: 398, alt: 'Revenant skill tree supplied by the site owner, showing its chosen utility skills and remaining points', caption: 'Revenant skill-tree example.' }} />
<h2 id="how-to-play">How to Play</h2>
<ol>
  <li>Keep <SkillIcon icon="SN_SIGHT" />True Sight, <SkillIcon icon="LK_PARRYING" />Shadow Parry, <SkillIcon icon="KG_KAGEMUSYA" />Darkside Shadow, and <SkillIcon icon="GN_BLOOD_SUCKER" />Vampire Mark active. Vampire Mark can also be cast on an ally for physical leech.</li>
  <li>Open with <SkillIcon icon="LK_SPIRALPIERCE" />Scythe Reap or <SkillIcon icon="KN_PIERCE" />Sweeping Slash to gain <strong>Combo Ready</strong>. Cast <SkillIcon icon="LG_MOONSLASHER" />Reaping Slash to build Overslash stacks, and keep using <SkillIcon icon="LK_SPIRALPIERCE" />Scythe Reap or <SkillIcon icon="KN_PIERCE" />Sweeping Slash to maintain <strong>Combo Ready</strong>. Cast <SkillIcon icon="LG_OVERBRAND" />Roaring Overslash while <strong>Combo Ready</strong> is active to boost its damage, with each Overslash stack adding another hit.</li>
  <li>You can also open with <SkillIcon icon="GC_DARKILLUSION" />Haunting Slice to close the gap. When it triggers <SkillIcon icon="LK_SPIRALPIERCE" />Scythe Reap, you gain <strong>Combo Ready</strong> and can follow the same combo above.</li>
  <li>Use <SkillIcon icon="RK_IGNITIONBREAK" />Hellraiser for <strong>Finisher Ready</strong>. With <strong>Combo Ready</strong> and at least one Overslash stack already active, <SkillIcon icon="LG_MOONSLASHER" />Reaping Slash can maximize your stacks.</li>
  <li>Keep attacking to leech HP and build the overheal barrier. Reposition out of ground damage. You can use <SkillIcon icon="RK_PHANTOMTHRUST" />Phantom Slice to bring distant targets into reach.</li>
</ol>
<h3>Quick combo rotation</h3>
<p><strong>Combo Ready</strong> opener (<SkillIcon icon="LK_SPIRALPIERCE" />Scythe Reap or <SkillIcon icon="KN_PIERCE" />Sweeping Slash) → <SkillIcon icon="LG_MOONSLASHER" />Reaping Slash → <SkillIcon icon="RK_IGNITIONBREAK" />Hellraiser → <SkillIcon icon="LG_MOONSLASHER" />Reaping Slash → <SkillIcon icon="KN_PIERCE" />Sweeping Slash → <SkillIcon icon="LG_OVERBRAND" />Roaring Overslash.</p>

<p>You can also open with <SkillIcon icon="GC_DARKILLUSION" />Haunting Slice, but it needs to trigger <SkillIcon icon="LK_SPIRALPIERCE" />Scythe Reap to grant <strong>Combo Ready</strong>. At max level, the trigger chance is 100%.</p>

<h2 id="leveling-spots">Leveling Spots</h2>
